msgid ""
"⟪k:0⟫⟪k:1⟫⟪k:2⟫⟪k:3⟫Three years back, there was a slave revolt at the lord’s manor. ⟪k:4⟫That’s "
"not ⟪k:5⟫quite⟪k:6⟫ accurate, though, ⟪k:7⟫because, while I was partly responsible for inciting "
"the riot, I wasn’t actually a slave.⟪k:8⟫⟪k:9⟫⟪k:10⟫⟪k:11⟫The local lord was spoken of—in whispers"
"—as the second coming of the great tyrant of old. ⟪k:12⟫The people were constantly grumbling "
"about how he seemed to treat the land like his own personal playground, exploiting everything and "
"everyone on it for his own amusement.⟪k:13⟫⟪k:14⟫⟪k:15⟫⟪k:16⟫When enough stress and resentment "
"builds up in a contained space, all it takes is a little shove from the outside to burst. ⟪k:17⟫"
"And that was our plan—me and a number of other dissatisfied citizens gathered together to pop "
"that bubble and give the lord a taste of how we felt about him."
